And then you and I,
we go outside and watch.

00:30:26.257 --> 00:30:27.158
JAY: Leave it to the lady?

00:30:27.192 --> 00:30:30.561
CESAR: Yes.
JAY: All right. Go get him.

00:30:30.594 --> 00:30:33.097
CESAR: Amanda must learn
how to teach Otto to stay in

00:30:33.130 --> 00:30:35.233
calm surrender on the bed.

00:30:35.266 --> 00:30:37.468
This allows him to be
emotionally detached from

00:30:37.501 --> 00:30:40.605
his pet parents, which
creates healthy boundaries.

00:30:40.638 --> 00:30:43.007
If Otto continues
disturbing her work,

00:30:43.040 --> 00:30:44.542
it could hurt her career.

00:30:49.280 --> 00:30:50.848
Amanda...

00:30:50.882 --> 00:30:53.017
 CESAR (over walkie-talkie):
 Looks like he's about
 to jump off the bed.

00:30:53.050 --> 00:30:54.485
 Confidently tell
 him to stay on the bed.

00:30:54.518 --> 00:30:56.120
AMANDA: Tsch.

00:30:57.588 --> 00:30:59.223
 CESAR (over walkie-talkie):
 He's still not settled.

00:30:59.256 --> 00:31:00.925
 Go make him stay.

00:31:02.593 --> 00:31:05.129
 Be clear with what
 you want him to do.

00:31:06.430 --> 00:31:08.900
AMANDA: Stay.

00:31:14.505 --> 00:31:15.973
CESAR: There you go.
There you go. That's good.

00:31:16.006 --> 00:31:17.208
JAY: That's good, right?
CESAR: Yup.

00:31:17.241 --> 00:31:18.509
There you go.

00:31:18.542 --> 00:31:19.743
She's a natural.

00:31:19.777 --> 00:31:22.980
Amanda was clear with what she
wanted and showed no hesitation

00:31:23.013 --> 00:31:24.481
and Otto did great.

00:31:24.515 --> 00:31:28.486
But now the real
challenge will be if Otto
can stay in a calm surrender

00:31:28.519 --> 00:31:33.358
when Amanda leaves the house or
will separation anxiety kick in?

00:31:35.125 --> 00:31:36.127
 CESAR (over walkie-talkie):
 All right, Amanda...

00:31:36.160 --> 00:31:37.328
CESAR: Come outside...

00:31:37.361 --> 00:31:38.496
 CESAR (over walkie-talkie):
 And just keep him there

00:31:38.529 --> 00:31:39.564
 before you leave.

00:31:39.597 --> 00:31:41.532
 He has to stay at
 calm surrender by himself.

00:31:41.565 --> 00:31:43.301
AMANDA: Uh-uh.

00:31:43.334 --> 00:31:45.703
CESAR: Teaching the dog to
understand the whole concept of

00:31:45.736 --> 00:31:48.373
separation is the
most difficult of all.

00:31:50.074 --> 00:31:51.575
AMANDA: Stay.

00:31:51.608 --> 00:31:53.912
CESAR: Confusion is the first
thing they, they go through.

00:31:56.046 --> 00:31:58.049
(whines)

00:31:59.550 --> 00:32:02.320
No, no, no, tsch, it's not good.

00:32:02.353 --> 00:32:03.421
Tsch.

00:32:06.724 --> 00:32:09.627
CESAR: Hey. Tsch.

00:32:11.628 --> 00:32:13.932
Tsch.

00:32:14.598 --> 00:32:18.135
(laughter)

00:32:18.168 --> 00:32:19.704
AMANDA: Not when
the big dog's in town.

00:32:19.737 --> 00:32:20.705
JAY: Oh, yeah.
CESAR: You see it?

00:32:20.738 --> 00:32:21.739
AMANDA: Yeah.

00:32:21.773 --> 00:32:22.707
CESAR: So that was
done just with eye contact.

00:32:22.740 --> 00:32:23.841
AMANDA: Yeah.
CESAR: Right?
JAY: Yeah.

00:32:23.875 --> 00:32:26.010
CESAR: So he's looking,
he's looking, like, "You again?"

00:32:26.043 --> 00:32:27.078
Yes.

00:32:27.111 --> 00:32:30.081
And that's when he moved back.

00:32:31.015 --> 00:32:33.117
Jay, send him back
just like I show you.

00:32:33.150 --> 00:32:37.588
JAY: Tsch. Tsch. Tsch.

00:32:39.156 --> 00:32:41.125
Tsch.

00:32:48.098 --> 00:32:49.200
CESAR: Not bad, Jay.

00:32:49.233 --> 00:32:50.535
But look at his energy.

00:32:50.568 --> 00:32:54.005
You can see the way
Otto's sitting up that
he's not calm surrender.

00:32:54.038 --> 00:32:56.607
We really need him
to lay down on the bed.

00:32:56.640 --> 00:32:59.343
That will tell me that he's
finally found the calm surrender

00:32:59.376 --> 00:33:02.380
that's been
missing from this pack.

00:33:03.714 --> 00:33:05.483
That's okay.
It takes repetition.

00:33:05.516 --> 00:33:08.019
Amanda, send him back.

00:33:08.652 --> 00:33:09.687
AMANDA: Tsch.

00:33:09.720 --> 00:33:11.555
CESAR: Yes!
JAY: Nice.

00:33:11.588 --> 00:33:13.391
CESAR: Yes, right there, yes.

00:33:13.424 --> 00:33:16.027
Oh, yes. Yes!

00:33:16.060 --> 00:33:17.561
You need a star,
like a little star.

00:33:17.594 --> 00:33:18.795
JAY: Yay.
AMANDA: I got a star.

00:33:18.829 --> 00:33:20.664
CESAR: That was your very best.
Yes, that was your very best.

00:33:20.697 --> 00:33:22.299
AMANDA: Woo-hoo.
CESAR: There you go.

00:33:22.332 --> 00:33:24.568
This is calm surrender.

00:33:24.601 --> 00:33:25.770
All right. Now, let's go in.

00:33:25.803 --> 00:33:26.971
AMANDA: We did it.

00:33:27.004 --> 00:33:27.972
JAY: I think the big thing
was just changing our energy,

00:33:28.005 --> 00:33:29.207
and being a little more
assertive with Otto and

00:33:29.240 --> 00:33:32.276
not being so hesitant because
we weren't sure what to do.

00:33:32.309 --> 00:33:34.612
But I think Cesar definitely
gave us more confidence.

00:33:34.645 --> 00:33:36.213
CESAR: This is what
you guys did with the,

00:33:36.246 --> 00:33:37.615
with the darken out the room.

00:33:37.648 --> 00:33:38.616
AMANDA: Yeah.
CESAR: Right?

00:33:38.649 --> 00:33:39.684
JAY: Yes.
AMANDA: Yeah.

00:33:39.717 --> 00:33:42.286
CESAR: So this is my
version of darken out the room,

00:33:42.319 --> 00:33:44.422
tell the brain to go
to calm surrender state.

00:33:44.455 --> 00:33:45.456
JAY: Yeah.
AMANDA: Okay.

00:33:45.489 --> 00:33:46.791
I think today went really well.

00:33:46.824 --> 00:33:49.060
I'm super proud of Otto.

00:33:49.093 --> 00:33:50.161
I'm super proud of us really.

00:33:50.194 --> 00:33:51.395
JAY: Yeah.

00:33:51.429 --> 00:33:53.731
AMANDA: I think we made a lot
of positive changes and a lot of

00:33:53.764 --> 00:33:58.302
progress and obviously that
will affect greatly my work.

00:33:58.335 --> 00:34:00.805
I'm really no
longer that worried about.

00:34:00.838 --> 00:34:01.739
JAY: Mm-hmm.

00:34:01.773 --> 00:34:03.507
AMANDA: You know,
my budding career and,

00:34:03.540 --> 00:34:07.078
and having him interrupt it,
so that's huge for me.

00:34:07.111 --> 00:34:09.246
JAY: I feel like we don't have
our little prison warden sort of

00:34:09.279 --> 00:34:11.482
running the show anymore.

00:34:11.515 --> 00:34:12.650
Yeah.

00:34:12.683 --> 00:34:13.617
AMANDA: Throwing out the
stripes and the orange suits,

00:34:13.650 --> 00:34:14.652
we're going out.

00:34:14.685 --> 00:34:16.320
JAY: Yeah.

00:34:17.588 --> 00:34:19.256
CESAR: Otto is a
very fast learner,

00:34:19.289 --> 00:34:21.325
and so are his pet parents.

00:34:21.358 --> 00:34:24.562
They're well on their
way to getting rid of
the separation anxiety

00:34:24.595 --> 00:34:26.764
that jeopardizes
Amanda's career.

00:34:26.797 --> 00:34:28.732
I have no doubt
they'll get there.

00:34:28.765 --> 00:34:31.702
Now, it's just
all about repetition.

00:34:34.872 --> 00:34:36.707
JAY: It's been a few weeks since
we've been at Cesar's ranch and

00:34:36.740 --> 00:34:39.276
Otto has done an amazing job,

00:34:39.309 --> 00:34:41.145
he's like a
completely different dog.

00:34:41.178 --> 00:34:43.247
AMANDA: I think
it's because we're
completely different parents.

00:34:43.280 --> 00:34:46.717
Cesar really helped us learn
how to be calm and confident

00:34:46.750 --> 00:34:49.420
with him, and it's
made all the difference.

00:34:49.453 --> 00:34:52.756
JAY: He's definitely
figured out how to use
his point of reference more.

00:34:52.789 --> 00:34:54.492
Stay.

00:34:54.525 --> 00:34:56.627
There's no more
invasion of space.

00:34:56.660 --> 00:34:57.728
AMANDA: Yeah.
JAY: And no more lying.

00:34:57.761 --> 00:34:58.729
AMANDA: Yeah.

00:34:58.762 --> 00:35:00.898
No more lying, he's been
so good during sessions,

00:35:00.931 --> 00:35:03.434
he still likes to be in the
room with me when I'm working,

00:35:03.467 --> 00:35:06.403
but he's really good
about sitting on his bed.

00:35:06.436 --> 00:35:10.241
We're so grateful
that it's changed and
gotten so much better.

00:35:10.274 --> 00:35:12.677
JAY: Thanks, Cesar.
AMANDA: Thank you, Cesar.

00:35:18.182 --> 00:35:20.417
 NARRATOR: Days after the
 breakthrough at the DPC,

00:35:20.450 --> 00:35:23.187
 Amanda and Simba continue
 their homework of building

00:35:23.220 --> 00:35:26.290
 and maintaining
 trust in one another.

00:35:26.323 --> 00:35:27.658
AMANDA: So the
homework is going pretty well,

00:35:27.691 --> 00:35:30.294
I still need a little bit
of help on the walk, but,

00:35:30.327 --> 00:35:32.229
you know, overall
feeling really good.

00:35:32.262 --> 00:35:34.765
GIL: Not 100% yet,
we're like 85% there.

00:35:34.798 --> 00:35:38.335
NARRATOR: The following week,
Cesar heads back to their home.

00:35:38.368 --> 00:35:42.240
Last time he was here, a nervous
bite led to desperate tears.

00:35:43.674 --> 00:35:45.309
AMANDA: Ow. Hey.

00:35:45.342 --> 00:35:47.478
CESAR: Did he bite?
AMANDA: Yeah, he did.

00:35:47.511 --> 00:35:50.481
So the first walk that we
did with Cesar on the first day

00:35:50.514 --> 00:35:51.582
was a challenge.

00:35:51.615 --> 00:35:53.217
I was not calm or confident,

00:35:53.250 --> 00:35:56.720
I was nervous and I was trying
to make it work, you know,

00:35:56.753 --> 00:35:59.557
with all my might but
it just, it just didn't.

00:35:59.590 --> 00:36:01.525
And it, it escalated.

00:36:01.558 --> 00:36:04.328
NARRATOR: Today, Cesar's hoping
to see the trust this pack needs

00:36:04.361 --> 00:36:07.231
 to ensure Simba's
 future is secure.

00:36:07.497 --> 00:36:08.866
AMANDA: Hi.
CESAR: Hi.

00:36:08.899 --> 00:36:09.967
GIL: Hey.
CESAR: How are you?

00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:10.835
AMANDA: How are you? Good.
CESAR: Good to see you.

00:36:10.868 --> 00:36:11.702
Good to see you.
What's up, brother?

00:36:11.735 --> 00:36:12.703
GIL: Brother,
good to see you, man.

00:36:12.736 --> 00:36:14.672
CESAR: Come on, I wanna
hear all the good news.

00:36:14.705 --> 00:36:15.806
(Amanda sighs)

00:36:15.840 --> 00:36:17.675
CESAR: I want good news.
AMANDA: Yes. It's been good.

00:36:17.708 --> 00:36:19.076
CESAR: Good.

00:36:19.110 --> 00:36:20.077
AMANDA: I still
need a little help on
the walks when other dogs

00:36:20.111 --> 00:36:23.447
come around, he, like,
is all over the place.

00:36:23.480 --> 00:36:26.617
He's not, he's not as much
listening to what I'm saying

00:36:26.650 --> 00:36:27.952
with the leash work.

00:36:27.985 --> 00:36:29.053
So that I still need work on.

00:36:29.086 --> 00:36:31.455
CESAR: Although Amanda
and Simba were able to build

00:36:31.488 --> 00:36:33.591
mutual trust at the DPC.

00:36:33.624 --> 00:36:36.427
AMANDA: What a
good boy, you did it.

00:36:36.460 --> 00:36:38.229
CESAR: It seems like
she's still getting nervous and

00:36:38.262 --> 00:36:40.531
having trust issues
during the walks.

00:36:40.564 --> 00:36:42.800
That's something we
must address right away.

00:36:42.833 --> 00:36:44.401
All right, let's see
the walk again, you join me.

00:36:44.434 --> 00:36:46.537
And, Amanda, get, get your boy.

00:36:46.570 --> 00:36:47.605
AMANDA: All right.
I will go get him.

00:36:47.638 --> 00:36:48.772
CESAR: All right. Let's do it.
AMANDA: All right.

00:36:48.806 --> 00:36:50.040
CESAR: Gil and I are gonna
stand at the end of the street,

00:36:50.074 --> 00:36:54.645
Amanda will walk Simba toward us
in front of the other dogs while

00:36:54.678 --> 00:36:57.248
I pinpoint where
the breakdown is.

00:36:57.281 --> 00:36:58.515
AMANDA: Let's
get the leash right.

00:36:58.548 --> 00:37:00.584
CESAR: Mm-hmm.
AMANDA: Get my hand around it.

00:37:00.617 --> 00:37:01.986
CESAR: Mm-hmm.
AMANDA: Okay. All right.

00:37:02.019 --> 00:37:03.921
Let's go.

00:37:03.954 --> 00:37:06.890
You know, the walk, I
didn't know how it was gonna go.

00:37:06.923 --> 00:37:08.959
I am a little bit nervous, um,

00:37:08.992 --> 00:37:12.363
but I, I really have been
working on just that trust

00:37:12.396 --> 00:37:15.032
and saying, it's gonna
be great, you're gonna do it.

00:37:15.065 --> 00:37:16.734
Are you ready?

00:37:16.767 --> 00:37:19.670
We're gonna do it very calmly.

00:37:19.703 --> 00:37:21.839
CESAR: Go ahead, guys.

00:37:28.979 --> 00:37:32.850
♪ ♪

00:37:32.883 --> 00:37:33.851
CESAR: Oh, this is good.

00:37:33.884 --> 00:37:34.852
This is good.

00:37:34.885 --> 00:37:36.553
Tail is up but he's not barking.

00:37:36.586 --> 00:37:40.258
AMANDA: Hey, hey, hey.

00:37:41.491 --> 00:37:44.528
Hey, hey, hey.

00:37:44.561 --> 00:37:45.663
CESAR: You're getting nervous.

00:37:45.696 --> 00:37:47.531
AMANDA: Hey.

00:37:47.564 --> 00:37:50.601
CESAR: Come on, Amanda,
don't focus on the dogs.

00:37:50.634 --> 00:37:52.536
Pull up on the leash.

00:37:54.705 --> 00:37:55.506
(growls)

00:37:55.539 --> 00:37:58.742
AMANDA: Hey. Hey.
That was enough.

00:37:58.775 --> 00:38:01.011
CESAR: She's definitely
controlling a little bit better.

00:38:01.044 --> 00:38:03.047
She's doing the physical aspect.

00:38:03.080 --> 00:38:05.949
The energy part is
not coming out yet.

00:38:05.982 --> 00:38:07.851
 NARRATOR: Since their
 breakthrough at the DPC,

00:38:07.884 --> 00:38:10.821
 Amanda and Simba continue to
 have difficulty trusting one

00:38:10.854 --> 00:38:15.059
another which has long been the
cause of nervous leadership and

00:38:15.092 --> 00:38:17.394
 a nervous aggression.

00:38:17.427 --> 00:38:21.065
AMANDA: Hey. Hey.

00:38:22.399 --> 00:38:23.600
CESAR: She's still nervous.

00:38:23.634 --> 00:38:26.704
The biggest problem I'm seeing
is that Amanda is not exhibiting

00:38:26.737 --> 00:38:29.606
the calm confident that
this pack needs from her.

00:38:29.639 --> 00:38:33.610
When she shakes the
nerves and starts to
trust herself as pack leader,

00:38:33.643 --> 00:38:36.580
Simba will have no choice
but to trust and follow.

00:38:36.613 --> 00:38:37.614
Pass it to me.

00:38:37.647 --> 00:38:38.815
AMANDA: Of course.
CESAR: Yeah.

00:38:38.848 --> 00:38:41.652
I'm gonna remind Amanda what
calm confidence looks like.

00:38:41.685 --> 00:38:44.455
Keep your shoulders back,
keep the leash short so

00:38:44.488 --> 00:38:46.357
he knows you're in charge.

00:38:47.291 --> 00:38:49.593
AMANDA: It's a short,
even shorter leash, I would say.

00:38:49.626 --> 00:38:51.495
GIL: That's even, yeah,
it's a lot shorter.

00:38:51.528 --> 00:38:53.864
CESAR: Mm-hmm. He was excited.

00:38:53.897 --> 00:38:55.299
GIL: Yeah.

00:38:55.332 --> 00:38:57.668
CESAR: But if he
gets too excited then he
wants to go and meet them.

00:38:57.701 --> 00:38:58.769
AMANDA: Got it.
CESAR: Let's do it again.

00:38:58.802 --> 00:39:01.071
AMANDA: Okay. Hey, hey.

00:39:01.104 --> 00:39:04.074
So the first walk,
you know, was a challenge.

00:39:04.107 --> 00:39:06.877
But Cesar was able to help
get that back on track and

00:39:06.910 --> 00:39:09.079
it's helpful to see that
in the moment because you're,

00:39:09.112 --> 00:39:10.247
you're in it.

00:39:10.280 --> 00:39:13.384
CESAR: Deep breath, calm
and confident, no excitement.

00:39:13.417 --> 00:39:15.386
AMANDA: Okay.

00:39:19.689 --> 00:39:21.058
CESAR: He's looking at the dogs.

00:39:21.091 --> 00:39:22.626
Keep him focused on the walk.

00:39:22.659 --> 00:39:25.129
AMANDA: Hey. Hey.

00:39:27.798 --> 00:39:29.800
CESAR: This is
really good right there.

00:39:29.833 --> 00:39:32.503
Look at the tail, see,
the tail is in the middle,

00:39:32.536 --> 00:39:33.504
bam, bam, bam.

00:39:33.537 --> 00:39:34.938
GIL: Yeah.

00:39:34.971 --> 00:39:36.540
CESAR: The tail
tells you the tale.

00:39:36.573 --> 00:39:38.142
AMANDA: Absolutely
night and day difference.

00:39:38.175 --> 00:39:39.477
It's a much better experience,

00:39:39.510 --> 00:39:45.149
just felt much more
under control and just
in charge of that walk.

00:39:45.182 --> 00:39:47.184
I knew I could do it,
I knew he could do it,

00:39:47.217 --> 00:39:48.619
I knew we could do it!

00:39:48.652 --> 00:39:49.520
CESAR: Mm-hmm. Nice.

00:39:49.553 --> 00:39:50.521
AMANDA: You know,
it like felt different.

00:39:50.554 --> 00:39:52.856
GIL: I am feeling that
calm energy right now.

00:39:52.889 --> 00:39:55.726
It does give me confidence
knowing that Simba and Amanda

00:39:55.759 --> 00:39:59.096
can trust each other and that
everybody knows their position

00:39:59.129 --> 00:40:00.998
and knows their role.

00:40:01.031 --> 00:40:02.566
CESAR: I think you're
ready for the final challenge.

00:40:02.599 --> 00:40:05.035
AMANDA: Follow.
(bleep), let's do it!

00:40:05.068 --> 00:40:06.703
CESAR: Let's go.

00:40:06.736 --> 00:40:08.539
See what a little
calm confidence can do for

00:40:08.572 --> 00:40:10.607
a nervous pack
leader like Amanda?

00:40:10.640 --> 00:40:12.209
Once she let go of her anxiety,

00:40:12.242 --> 00:40:14.711
Simba was able to
trust her calmly.

00:40:14.744 --> 00:40:17.481
So now it's time for
their final challenge.

00:40:19.115 --> 00:40:21.051
All right.

00:40:21.084 --> 00:40:23.954
The goal is to
bring family members to
have a gathering, right?

00:40:23.987 --> 00:40:26.723
And, Amanda, you're
gonna have my boy over there.

00:40:26.756 --> 00:40:28.692
No touch, no talk,
no eye contact, you guys.

00:40:28.725 --> 00:40:29.993
AMANDA: All right.
CESAR: Can sit over there.
GIL: Sounds good.

00:40:30.026 --> 00:40:30.994
CESAR: And you put
your boy over there.

00:40:31.027 --> 00:40:32.295
AMANDA: Okay.

00:40:32.329 --> 00:40:34.531
CESAR: When I first met
Simba, he was crated
in the living room.

00:40:34.564 --> 00:40:35.933
(barking)

00:40:35.966 --> 00:40:37.101
AMANDA: Oh, Simba.

00:40:37.134 --> 00:40:39.503
CESAR: Acting aggressively
toward anyone who came into

00:40:39.536 --> 00:40:41.605
Amanda's intimate space.

00:40:41.638 --> 00:40:43.073
AMANDA: I don't let him
out when he's like this.

00:40:43.106 --> 00:40:46.143
CESAR: And the house was
full of fear and distrust.

00:40:46.176 --> 00:40:48.946
Now that he and Amanda
have put in the work together,

00:40:48.979 --> 00:40:51.081
it's time to see how
Simba reacts to something

00:40:51.114 --> 00:40:54.151
Amanda hasn't seen
in months, houseguests.

00:40:55.986 --> 00:40:57.588
AMANDA: So I haven't had
family over in a long time,

00:40:57.621 --> 00:41:00.057
you know, because of
the way Simba has been.

00:41:00.090 --> 00:41:02.559
I, I, I was nervous,
I was anxious about it.

00:41:02.592 --> 00:41:05.996
So it'd be really great if we
could practice some of that, so.

00:41:06.029 --> 00:41:06.997
CESAR: Yup.
AMANDA: I'm excited.

00:41:07.030 --> 00:41:07.998
CESAR: We will, we will.

00:41:08.031 --> 00:41:10.968
Melanie, come on out.

00:41:11.001 --> 00:41:12.970
GIL: She got this.

00:41:16.606 --> 00:41:17.641
MELANIE: Hey!

00:41:17.674 --> 00:41:22.212
CESAR: He knows her.
AMANDA: Hey, hey, hey. Hey.

00:41:22.245 --> 00:41:24.715
CESAR: Very good. Very good.

00:41:24.748 --> 00:41:26.149
AMANDA: Sit. Sit.

00:41:26.182 --> 00:41:28.252
All the way down.

00:41:28.518 --> 00:41:30.254
All right, so we
just no touch, no talk,

00:41:30.287 --> 00:41:32.523
no eye contact, we're
gonna let him be calm.

00:41:32.556 --> 00:41:33.791
CESAR: Beautiful.

00:41:33.824 --> 00:41:34.725
MELANIE: It's good to see you.
CESAR: It's a big difference.

00:41:34.758 --> 00:41:37.160
AMANDA: Yeah.
CESAR: That was beautiful.

00:41:37.193 --> 00:41:38.962
Okay. Mom, you're up next.

00:41:38.995 --> 00:41:40.964
Come on out.

00:41:40.997 --> 00:41:42.533
WOMAN: Amanda!
AMANDA: Hi.

00:41:42.566 --> 00:41:43.700
WOMAN: I'm so
excited to see you.

00:41:43.733 --> 00:41:44.868
AMANDA: Hey, hey.
CESAR: There you go.

00:41:44.901 --> 00:41:45.869
This is good.

00:41:45.902 --> 00:41:46.703
WOMAN: Oh, good to see you.

00:41:46.736 --> 00:41:47.737
CESAR: So I
heard you might be...

00:41:47.771 --> 00:41:49.139
WOMAN: Oh my God, I
can't believe you're here.

00:41:49.172 --> 00:41:50.674
I've watched every episode!

00:41:50.707 --> 00:41:52.309
(laughter)

00:41:52.342 --> 00:41:53.543
CESAR: Thank you.

00:41:53.577 --> 00:41:55.812
WOMAN: Thank you for making
us better humans for our dogs.

00:41:55.845 --> 00:41:58.582
CESAR: Oh, look at her,
she's plugging the show.

00:41:58.615 --> 00:41:59.583
Make yourself at home.

00:41:59.616 --> 00:42:00.417
WOMAN: Oh.
CESAR: Yeah.

00:42:00.450 --> 00:42:01.418
Please, please,
that was perfect.

00:42:01.451 --> 00:42:02.085
AMANDA: He's doing good.
CESAR: That was perfect.

00:42:02.119 --> 00:42:03.587
That was, that was amazing.

00:42:03.620 --> 00:42:04.788
AMANDA: He's doing great.

00:42:04.821 --> 00:42:06.890
GIL: Incredibly shocked about
how calm Simba actually is

00:42:06.923 --> 00:42:10.127
right now and I am
extremely proud of my wife.

00:42:10.160 --> 00:42:11.295
CESAR: All right.
Where's your dad?

00:42:11.328 --> 00:42:12.996
AMANDA: Hello.
MAN: How cool is this?

00:42:13.029 --> 00:42:14.598
AMANDA: Dad, thank you.
CESAR: Oh, look at that.

00:42:14.631 --> 00:42:15.566
MAN: Hello.

00:42:15.599 --> 00:42:16.733
GIL: All the family
coming over the house,

00:42:16.767 --> 00:42:18.869
and getting close to her,
and he's not doing anything.

00:42:18.902 --> 00:42:20.837
So it's great to see.

00:42:20.870 --> 00:42:22.706
MAN: He's good, you're, hey.
I love it!

00:42:22.739 --> 00:42:23.774
CESAR: Thank you.

00:42:23.807 --> 00:42:24.875
MAN: I'd like to hug
my granddaughter, is that okay?

00:42:24.908 --> 00:42:25.776
CESAR: Yeah. Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.
Do it, do it, do it.

00:42:25.809 --> 00:42:26.343
MAN: All right.
I'm going to hug her.

00:42:26.376 --> 00:42:28.312
CESAR: Oh, I love it.

00:42:28.345 --> 00:42:29.213
Well, look at that.

00:42:29.246 --> 00:42:31.348
AMANDA: This would
never have happened.

00:42:31.381 --> 00:42:34.184
We would never have family
get-togethers because it would

00:42:34.217 --> 00:42:36.086
be out of control,
it's like chaos.

00:42:36.119 --> 00:42:37.788
It's just totally
a different energy,

00:42:37.821 --> 00:42:41.858
and just more in
control and more confident.

00:42:41.891 --> 00:42:44.294
And he's able to just chill.

00:42:44.327 --> 00:42:46.730
And, you know,
it's a little shocking.

00:42:46.763 --> 00:42:50.033
I'm, I was, you know, I
am super excited about that.

00:42:50.066 --> 00:42:53.937
I'm really excited to see
how far we can get with this.

00:42:53.970 --> 00:42:56.373
How much he can be calm,
how much he can trust,

00:42:56.406 --> 00:42:57.774
and it just feels good.

00:42:57.807 --> 00:42:59.876
I'm the leader of the pack.

00:42:59.909 --> 00:43:03.180
SIENNA: I'm so glad that
Simba is much more calm now and

00:43:03.213 --> 00:43:05.148
I thank you for
your help so much.

00:43:05.181 --> 00:43:06.349
CESAR: My pleasure.

00:43:06.382 --> 00:43:11.822
SIENNA: And I hope to have more
people over in my lifetime.

00:43:11.855 --> 00:43:13.757
CESAR: Mm-hmm. Your lifetime.

00:43:16.326 --> 00:43:17.995
SIENNA: Oh, gosh, yes,
it's changed my life.

00:43:18.028 --> 00:43:19.763
I love having a dog.

00:43:19.796 --> 00:43:24.001
Simba is my best friend,
even closer to a brother.

00:43:24.034 --> 00:43:26.937
It's a lot more fun
when Simba's around.

00:43:26.970 --> 00:43:29.239
CESAR: I am really
proud of Amanda and Simba.

00:43:29.272 --> 00:43:33.377
Now they share a
special bond that is
deeply rooted in mutual trust.

00:43:33.410 --> 00:43:36.380
And today is the first day
of the rest of their happy,

00:43:36.413 --> 00:43:38.248
peaceful life together.

00:43:38.281 --> 00:43:40.017
To me, this is a perfect day.

00:43:40.050 --> 00:43:41.118
Thank you for trusting me.

00:43:41.151 --> 00:43:42.819
AMANDA: Thank you so much.
CESAR: Thank you, guys.

00:43:42.852 --> 00:43:43.820
AMANDA: I would
do some high fives!

00:43:43.853 --> 00:43:46.023
GIL: Thank you.

00:43:46.056 --> 00:43:47.958
CESAR: Trust, respect, love.

00:43:47.991 --> 00:43:50.794
To me, that's always been
the moral code which forms

00:43:50.827 --> 00:43:53.096
a powerful bond with your dog.

00:43:53.129 --> 00:43:55.899
There is a reason trust
comes first because that is

00:43:55.932 --> 00:43:59.736
the foundation
of any relationship
not just with your dog.

00:43:59.769 --> 00:44:03.106
So it is important to teach your
dog to trust and respect you.

00:44:03.139 --> 00:44:06.677
And once you have that, your
pack will be all about love.

00:44:08.278 --> 00:44:09.313
 

